Day 06 of my bug bounty series: exploring the OWASP Top 10.

Every hunter hears about it. Today I finally sat down and read it properly.

Here are the 4 I focused on first:

1. OWASP Top 10: a list of the most critical web security risks.
2. Injection: what happens when untrusted input changes how an application behaves.
3. Broken access control: users reaching things they shouldn't be able to.
4. Security misconfiguration: simple setup mistakes that weaken everything else.

The list isn't a checklist to memorize. It's a map of where to look.

